1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Aegis Pocket: Approve AI agents, safely, from your pocket.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:08,600
Posture at a glance: Pending approvals, threats blocked, personal data redacted and budget left. All numbers are mock data simulated on the device.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:12,600
An agent asks: A simulated agent request arrives (mock data). The app posts a local notification and shows an in-app banner.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,800
Open it from the shade: Tapping the notification opens that exact request through a WantAgent deep link.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:23,800
Why a human is asked: A 0-100 risk score with plain-language reasons, computed on the phone. The agent's own note is labelled untrusted and never scored.

6
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,800
A $50 subscription: This one needs an admin. Acting as Emily (admin); a sponsor can never approve their own agent's request.

7
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:34,000
Step-up before approving: Approve first asks for face, fingerprint or PIN. The emulator has no authenticator, so the app shows its labelled manual fallback.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Decision recorded: Approved after the manual confirmation; the pending count drops. Denying never asks for authentication.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,400
What data leaves: The built-in synthetic sample: email, phone, PESEL, IBAN and card number become [EMAIL_1], [PESEL_1]... placeholders, on the phone.

10
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,600
On the home screen: The AI posture widget (MOCK badge) shows what is waiting, updated by the app.

11
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,000
github.com/JustAnotherDevv/tiles-hackyeah-2026: Recorded on the DevEco HarmonyOS emulator. Requests, agents and numbers are mock data simulated on the device.
